{
  "id": "Compound::DB06738 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Ketobemidone is likely to interact with Cyp2c8 through a shared pathway involving cytochrome P450 enzymes. The evidence suggests that Ketobemidone binds to Cyp2c9, which is involved in oxidoreductive activities, and this activity is also recognized by Cyp2c8. This implies a potential functional overlap between Cyp2c9 and Cyp2c8 in metabolizing substrates, particularly those involving quinone or similar acceptors. The presence of multiple pathways linking Ketobemidone to Cyp2c8, through Cyp2c9 and Cyp3a4, highlights a broader role in metabolic processes, possibly involving the oxidation of diverse chemical substrates. The integration of these pathways suggests that Ketobemidone may influence Cyp2c8 through a mechanism involving enzyme activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
